 He served in the House throughout, so the vote counts as in-term. Voting against a ban only shows which side he is on. It doesn't pick between rungs 1, 2 and 3.\n- **Forum, 2026:** at a candidate forum during the current campaign, he says in his own words that he killed the marriage amendment in committee. He also speaks against attacks on \"marriage equality\". This also shows only his side. It names no anti-discrimination clause and no position on a religious exemption. I classed it `statement-other` because the moderator's question isn't in the transcript.\n- **Bill details page:** it is coded as part of the same HJR 3 vote record. It prints neither his vote nor the House tally.\n- **`needs_source`:** his own words, or his record, on a broad sexual-orientation anti-discrimination measure. That is what could separate rung 1 (equality plus discrimination protection) from rung 2 (equal marriage).\n- **Quote:** one candidate quote, \"I'm not participating in this cynical, hateful process.\" I tiered it `none` and marked it not quotable, because it looks back at a past act rather than saying what he would do (`not-forward`).","ttft_ms":14300,"type":"result","duration_ms":35523,"uuid":"a5555fc6-d903-408f-b46f-d816f2efe517","ttft_stream_ms":1994,"time_to_request_ms":357,"first_content_frame_ms":1995,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
